#   file 5.46 (Debian 13) can't handle one entry: it must have zero or two+.
#   So we add this bogus entry just to make it stop complaining.
#   The following offset is well past  FILE_BYTES_MAX (7 MiB),
#   so the test is unreachable by construction
0x7f000000 string \xff\xfe\xff\xfe\xff\xfe\xff\xfe SHOULD NEVER MATCH; file a bug

#   Newish magic numbers that are not yet in many LTS releases.

# New format OpenSSH private keys.
0	string	-----BEGIN\ OPENSSH\ PRIVATE\ KEY-	OpenSSH private key
